c Petersen graph minimum vertex cover instance (10 vertices, 15 edges, all weights 1).
c Encoding: variable v is true when vertex v is picked into the cover.
c   hard clause (u v)              for every edge (u, v): at least one endpoint is picked
c   soft clause (-v) with weight 1 for every vertex: pay 1 for each picked vertex
c Lower bound: a 5-vertex cover would need 5*3 = 15 edge slots for 15 edges, so the
c picked vertices would have to span no edge at all; but the Petersen graph has
c independence number 4, so no such 5-set exists. The solver returns a 6-vertex
c cover, hence the optimum is exactly 6.
p wcnf 10 25 2
